- d1 `packages/coding-agent/src/session/session-manager.ts` forkFrom options parameter type: **combined**. The fork API must accept both sides' knobs: L14's branch scoping (`sourceLeafId`) and R's `copyArtifacts`, `resetInheritedCost`, `repairInterruptedTail`, `seance`. Dropping either removes a supported call (task/executor.ts passes sourceLeafId; session-transfer.ts passes repairInterruptedTail; seance callers pass seance/copyArtifacts).
- d2 `packages/coding-agent/src/session/session-manager.ts` forkFrom history selection body: **combined**. Branch scoping must run first (it decides which entries are inherited), then R's usage normalization and optional cost reset must apply to exactly that inherited set so a branch-scoped fork gets the same zero/normalized usage treatment R gives full forks, and neither pass touches entries the fork does not copy.
- d3 `packages/coding-agent/src/session/session-manager.ts` forkBranch method and forkFrom private helpers: **combined**. L's `forkBranch` (storage-aware instance entry point that forwards sourceLeafId) and R's three private fork helpers are independent additions at the same insertion point; both are needed, so both are kept, forkBranch first to stay adjacent to forkFrom as L had it.
- d4 `packages/coding-agent/src/session/session-manager.ts` forkFrom doc comment: **combined**. The documentation must describe every option the reconciled signature accepts: L's named-agent `sessionFile` rationale and sourceLeafId scoping, plus R's artifact-copy default and seance semantics.
- d5 `packages/coding-agent/test/session/session-manager-fork.test.ts` imports from session-storage: **theirs**. R's import is a strict superset of L's (it adds FileSessionStorage, used by the retained R tests); L's MemorySessionStorage remains imported, so both sides' tests compile.
- d6 `packages/coding-agent/test/session/session-manager-fork.test.ts` describe(\"SessionManager.forkFrom\") test bodies: **combined**. Both sides add distinct tests to the same describe block; keeping only one side would drop coverage of the other side's obligations. All assertions are retained verbatim, with L's second test's closing brace restored since the shared trailing `});` only closes one test.
- d7 `packages/coding-agent/src/export/html/tool-views.generated.js` all: **theirs**. This path is a left-only build artifact (banner: "Auto-generated by packages/collab-web/scripts/build-tool-views.ts - DO NOT EDIT"), byte-identical (sha256 8112a48a…) to left's gitignored copy. Right replaced that pipeline with the content-addressed shared viewer: packages/collab-web/scripts/build-export-viewer.ts writes packages/coding-agent/export-assets/export-viewer-<hash>.js plus the committed manifest packages/coding-agent/src/export/html/viewer.generated.json, and src/export/html/index.ts inlines that bundle for the <omp-tool-view> component used by template.js. In the merged tree the left generator (packages/collab-web/scripts/build-tool-views.ts) does not exist, nothing imports or loads tool-views.generated.js (only the conflicted left half of packages/coding-agent/package.json mentions a dist/tool-views.generated-*.js glob), and right's .gitignore no longer ignores it, so leaving it would commit a stale 284 KB orphan blob. Deleting it keeps the merged tree on right's viewer pipeline; no regeneration is possible or needed because the generator that produced it is gone. R224 (assistant content timeline) is unaffected: it lives in template.js, which is right's version and walks msg.content once in block order (template.js:1176-1199).
- d8 `packages/coding-agent/package.json` all: **theirs**. Upstream restructured the manifest wholesale (v18.18.7, oxlint/oxfmt scripts, gen:export-viewer/gen:rpc, new exports, @oh-my-pi/omptype dep) and dropped the dependencies the fork still listed (turndown, mammoth, linkedom, chalk, zod, lru-cache, handlebars, fast-xml-parser, @mozilla/readability, @xterm/headless, arktype, header-generator, @puppeteer/browsers, @agentclientprotocol/sdk, @oh-my-pi/hashline, mupdf, marked, sherpa-onnx-node, @huggingface/transformers). None of those are imported by merged source, and the merged root catalog (with R88's kitty-vt-wasm entry) no longer defines them, so keeping the fork's `catalog:` entries would make the manifest invalid and block `bun install --frozen-lockfile` (the `marked@catalog:` blocker). The fork's only manifest change, the `test:screenshot:fullscreen` vhs script for its fullscreen-chat feature, is kept on top of upstream's scripts block.
- d9 `packages/coding-agent/src/cli.ts` imports (line 31-39) and worker-host dispatch (line 543-552): **combined**. Both sides changed the same two regions for independent reasons. Upstream replaced the static `./cli/profile-alias` import with the lazy `@oh-my-pi/pi-natives/sqlite-locks` install call plus `isNativeShell`/`runNativeShell` (profile-alias is now dynamically imported at the `--alias` boundary), and made worker dispatch overlap `setFullProcessName()`. The fork added `applySubprocessNiceness(...)` before worker dispatch so worker subprocesses get their niceness applied. Keeping upstream's import set and its Promise.all dispatch while running the fork's niceness call first preserves both: the nit miceness hook still precedes dispatch, and upstream's sqlite-lock shim / native-shell branches stay intact.
- d10 `packages/coding-agent/src/cli/session-picker.ts` all (file deleted): **theirs**. Upstream deleted the fork-local picker and moved the behavior into `@oh-my-pi/pi-tui/apps/session-picker` (`selectSession(sessions, options, host)`), which the merged `main.ts` already uses through `loadSessionPicker()`. The replacement is a superset of the deleted file: it keeps the fullscreen alt-screen overlay anchored top-left at 100% (mouse tracking is still enabled because a fullscreen overlay defaults to it in `TUI`), the history matcher, delete, all-projects scope, title/scopeLabel/showCwd, and adds pins, rename, completeSessions and `listAllForPicker`. Nothing in the merged tree imports `./cli/session-picker`, so deleting it loses no fork behavior and avoids a duplicate picker implementation.
